# Project core

## Workflow

- Large features: write plan in `docs/superpowers/plans/` before coding.
- End every change set with `bash scripts/verify.sh`.
- Security/provisioning changes: `t/test_security_guards.pl` and `t/test_provisioning_flow.pl` must stay green.
- Webmin-only target: ship via `.wbm`; do not maintain deb/rpm packaging unless explicitly requested.

## Code and UI

- UI strings: German in `src/lang/de` + `src/lang/en`.
- Code/comments: English.
- Only `ui_*` for UI; no hardcoded colors/styles.
- `ui_submit` with explicit CSS class (5th arg): `btn-danger` destructive, `btn-default` neutral.
- New error text keys in **both** lang files.
- No hardcoded paths outside the module; resolve Webmin CLI tools dynamically.

## Commits

- Use local git config as author.
- Do not commit unless the user asks.

## Integrations page

- `integrations.cgi`: Steam (accounts, SteamCMD), download-source API keys (Modrinth contact, CurseForge key, optional Hangar token, custom URL hosts), debug logging.
- Module config keys: `modrinth_contact`, `curseforge_api_key`, `hangar_api_token`, `download_allow_custom_url`, `download_custom_hosts`, `debug_logging`.
- Config file: `/etc/webmin/linuxgsm-webcore/config` — CGIs use `module_config_sync_in()`; **game-user workers** read integration keys from `$job_dir/.worker_secrets` (written at dispatch via `write_job_worker_secrets()`). Standalone Perl also calls `module_config_bootstrap_standalone($module_root)` with `WEBCORE_JOB_DIR` set.

## Background jobs (summary)

- All long tasks → job + **`job_live.cgi`** (see `instance-jobs.mdc`, `workers-shell.mdc`).
- Minecraft mods/modpacks/Java/reinstall: see `minecraft-mods.mdc` (`mods.cgi`, not manage blocks).
- Success only after `$JOB_DIR/status` = `ok` (see `no-blind-success-feedback.mdc`).
